Package: CanardAbsurd
Title: Checkpointed R Workflows over 'DuckDB' and 'Quack'
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Sounkou Mahamane", "Toure", email = "sounkoutoure@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Runs durable R tasks using 'DuckDB' for state and the 'Quack'
    extension for remote Structured Query Language (SQL) access. Provides
    database hosting, leased task claims,
    checkpoint replay, retries, durable sleeps, and a pull-based R worker.
    External side effects require application-level idempotency.
License: GPL (>= 2)
URL: https://rgenomicsetl.github.io/CanardAbsurd/,
    https://github.com/RGenomicsETL/CanardAbsurd
BugReports: https://github.com/RGenomicsETL/CanardAbsurd/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.3.0)
Imports: DBI, duckdb (>= 1.5.3), jsonlite, S7, stats
Suggests: callr, tinytest, roxygen2, s7contract (>= 0.2.1), withr,
    knitr, rmarkdown, parallelly
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/Needs/website: pkgdown, litedown
Config/Needs/graphics: rsvg
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: The JSON extension matching the installed DuckDB runtime;
    the matching Quack extension for remote clients and database hosting
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
